261
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:58,124
- Very strange. 
- Good that you noticed.

262
00:27:59,678 --> 00:28:01,339
A hug then.

263
00:28:09,646 --> 00:28:11,762
You smell great.

264
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,607
- See you tomorrow. 
- See you tomorrow.

265
00:30:06,013 --> 00:30:07,970
What are you doing this weekend?

266
00:30:08,849 --> 00:30:10,886
I don't know. Gardening.

267
00:30:11,018 --> 00:30:14,886
Gardening? Cool. 
Have a great time.

268
00:31:20,962 --> 00:31:24,171
Come on! The West!

269
00:31:24,299 --> 00:31:27,792
You must catch up on English. 
Pick up the pace!

270
00:31:27,886 --> 00:31:30,173
Those who do not cycle may jog.

271
00:32:30,407 --> 00:32:36,779
Anita // 16.52 
Thanks for last time. Hanging out tonight?

272
00:32:42,461 --> 00:32:45,203
Markus
Sorry

273
00:32:50,218 --> 00:32:53,882
Marcus 
Going to play a match in Drammen :(

274
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:06,975
Anita - How about next week? 
We can cook pizza.

275
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:08,854
Read

276
00:34:11,925 --> 00:34:15,007
Hey, you came anyway. 
Are you feeling better?

277
00:34:15,094 --> 00:34:17,837
- Much better. 
- Come in.

278
00:34:19,306 --> 00:34:21,514
How nice.

279
00:34:21,601 --> 00:34:25,686
we just ate 
so if you are hungry…

280
00:34:25,772 --> 00:34:27,853
No, thanks.

281
00:34:27,983 --> 00:34:31,021
But you might want some wine?

282
00:34:31,110 --> 00:34:33,978
No, thanks. I don't drink.

283
00:34:37,284 --> 00:34:42,654
Girls, now you have to say hello to Anita.

284
00:34:47,168 --> 00:34:51,286
Anita and I are 
old gym buddies.

285
00:34:51,339 --> 00:34:54,081
Then she suddenly appeared 
as Markus' teacher.

286
00:34:54,175 --> 00:34:59,090
And Robin's teacher. 
He has talked a lot about you.

287
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:02,013
- What good. Anita Lønstrup. 
- Jenny.

288
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:06,014
My colleagues at the Norwegian Food Safety Authority, 
Randi and Anne.

289
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:09,313
- Anita. 
- Randi.

290
00:35:09,399 --> 00:35:13,688
Finally we have Eli, 
who lives further down the street.

291
00:35:13,778 --> 00:35:16,770
- Nice. 
- Sit down.

292
00:35:16,865 --> 00:35:18,731
- Sit here. 
- It's free here.

293
00:35:18,825 --> 00:35:21,908
Are you ready for some dessert?

294
00:35:22,037 --> 00:35:25,826
I have baked cheesecake. 
Without palm oil this time.

295
00:35:25,915 --> 00:35:27,906
Fantastic.

296
00:35:29,377 --> 00:35:32,790
So you are the bookworms?

297
00:35:32,881 --> 00:35:34,588
Yes, we are.

298
00:35:34,674 --> 00:35:40,386
There were more of us, but people drop out, 
for various reasons.

299
00:35:41,514 --> 00:35:45,348
- What are you reading? 
- "Without a Thread" by Jens Bjørneboe.

300
00:35:45,435 --> 00:35:47,847
Is it good, or?

301
00:35:47,979 --> 00:35:51,813
I think it was very good. 
Entertainment in any case.

302
00:35:51,900 --> 00:35:54,892
It was more reminiscent of youth.

303
00:35:55,028 --> 00:35:58,362
There are so many black souls.

304
00:35:58,448 --> 00:36:00,655
- People are completely... 
- Yes.

305
00:36:00,742 --> 00:36:05,487
I thought it would be 
much more explicit.

306
00:36:05,580 --> 00:36:07,571
It was banned.

307
00:36:07,666 --> 00:36:09,782
It still is.

308
00:36:09,876 --> 00:36:14,495
You should read "Sodom's 120 Days" 
by Marquis de Sade.

309
00:36:16,216 --> 00:36:18,048
- Is it new? 
- No.

310
00:36:18,134 --> 00:36:21,297
It is very old, 
from the 18th century.

311
00:36:22,305 --> 00:36:24,512
1700, then it is very old.

312
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:27,057
Then I don't know if I can take it.

313
00:36:27,143 --> 00:36:31,353
- How did the match go? 
- Good.

314
00:36:31,439 --> 00:36:33,146
- Did you win? 
- A draw.

315
00:36:33,233 --> 00:36:35,520
- Come and say hello. 
- Is it Markus?

316
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:38,978
There we have the soccer star.

317
00:36:39,072 --> 00:36:40,654
How big he has become.

318
00:36:40,740 --> 00:36:44,028
His father up in the day.

319
00:36:44,119 --> 00:36:46,531
Did you score?

320
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:50,831
- I mostly sat on the bench. 
- He's not in shape.

321
00:36:52,085 --> 00:36:56,830
I can't hold myself. 
I have to give you a hug.

322
00:36:56,923 --> 00:36:59,631
You have grown so big!

323
00:36:59,718 --> 00:37:02,130
They are soaring.

324
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:05,429
Where do the years go?

325
00:37:05,557 --> 00:37:08,390
You two know each other.

326
00:37:08,518 --> 00:37:11,385
It has happened 
some PE lessons now.

327
00:37:11,521 --> 00:37:15,185
Both ghost ball and other activities.

328
00:37:15,275 --> 00:37:19,189
I just said that Robin brags about 
how much fun you have in the lessons.

329
00:37:19,279 --> 00:37:22,021
It is very nice.

330
00:37:22,115 --> 00:37:24,573
Why are you here?

331
00:37:25,243 --> 00:37:28,031
- Why am I here? 
- Yes?

332
00:37:29,914 --> 00:37:32,497
You'll have to ask your mother.

333
00:37:32,584 --> 00:37:34,791
I invited her to the book club.

334
00:37:34,878 --> 00:37:39,543
- I thought it might fit. 
- It's very fun.

335
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:42,545
I have to shower. 
You can have such a nice time.

336
00:37:43,595 --> 00:37:45,177
He is so beautiful.

337
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:51,134
- Does he have a girlfriend? 
- No, he doesn't seem that interested.

338
00:37:51,227 --> 00:37:53,184
You know that, right?

339
00:37:54,314 --> 00:37:56,806
- What? 
- Because you are his teacher.

340
00:37:57,525 --> 00:38:00,813
- Excuse me? 
- If he has a girlfriend.

341
00:38:01,905 --> 00:38:04,693
I don't know anything about that.

342
00:38:04,783 --> 00:38:07,525
- But I don't think so. 
- It's coming.

343
00:38:09,245 --> 00:38:11,828
How about love for you?

344
00:38:15,251 --> 00:38:17,288
You get straight to the point.

345
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:20,166
It's going well.

346
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:22,915
- You're not single? 
- No, I'm married.

347
00:38:23,051 --> 00:38:25,793
Were there any children?

348
00:38:25,887 --> 00:38:29,505
Hasse, as he is called, 
have two adult daughters.

349
00:38:30,558 --> 00:38:33,141
- Are you all right? 
- It works very well.

350
00:38:33,228 --> 00:38:35,890
Someone has it.

351
00:38:36,022 --> 00:38:39,390
Don't start now.

352
00:38:40,527 --> 00:38:43,235
- Did you have more wine? 
- Yes, I have more wine.

353
00:38:44,697 --> 00:38:47,530
Unni, do you have a toilet?

354
00:38:47,617 --> 00:38:51,110
Up the stairs and to the left.

355
00:40:02,692 --> 00:40:05,810
- Hello? 
- It's me.

356
00:40:08,573 --> 00:40:10,530
Anita.

357
00:41:30,446 --> 00:41:33,404
Sorry, didn't mean to.

358
00:41:35,451 --> 00:41:39,410
- There is a toilet further down the hall. 
- Thank you.

359
00:42:31,090 --> 00:42:35,129
“Obviously I wanted to go out straight away 
and look at the city"-

360
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:38,382
-"but a promise is a promise 
and I stayed in my room."

361
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:42,974
“I bathed, washed myself 
thoroughly everywhere…”

362
00:42:44,020 --> 00:42:46,603
"...and went to bed with a book."

363
00:42:46,689 --> 00:42:50,227
"It was 'Fiskerjenten' by Bjørnson.

364
00:42:50,318 --> 00:42:53,436
"If the travel fund was increased 
with 5000 Norwegian kroner"-

365
00:42:53,571 --> 00:42:55,812
- "everything would change."

366
00:42:55,907 --> 00:42:59,070
“Actually, I should thank you 
Dr. Petterson for everything."

367
00:42:59,160 --> 00:43:03,779
“I thought it would have been nice 
to have him here in bed."

368
00:43:03,873 --> 00:43:06,706
“Just lie in his arms 
and have a good time."

369
00:43:08,127 --> 00:43:10,368
“I think I was dreaming 
about him that night."

370
00:43:10,505 --> 00:43:12,291
It's so nice.

371
00:43:12,381 --> 00:43:15,294
- Do you think it was nice? 
- Delicious.

372
00:43:16,677 --> 00:43:18,293
Where did you go?

373
00:43:18,387 --> 00:43:21,095
Sorry, I was feeling 
suddenly not good.

374
00:43:21,182 --> 00:43:24,516
I just needed some air 
and water on the face.

375
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:28,061
- But now I feel better. 
- Eat some cheesecake.

376
00:43:29,065 --> 00:43:30,521
It was delicious.

377
00:43:30,608 --> 00:43:32,645
You must be good at baking.

378
00:43:34,028 --> 00:43:36,816
I am very fond of that one.

379
00:43:44,330 --> 00:43:47,994
- Was it good? 
- I will be completely...

380
00:43:48,084 --> 00:43:49,791
You seem healthier now.

381
00:43:49,877 --> 00:43:53,165
- I became very energetic. 
- What do you have in the cake?

382
00:44:12,066 --> 00:44:15,024
Marcus: 
Isn't that the song from Armageddon?

383
00:44:15,111 --> 00:44:17,853
Anita: 
What is it?

384
00:44:17,989 --> 00:44:20,981
Marcus: 
A movie

385
00:44:21,075 --> 00:44:23,817
Anita: 
We have to see it

386
00:44:34,797 --> 00:44:38,210
Mine. Mike. Trick.

387
00:44:38,301 --> 00:44:39,712
- Robin.

388
00:44:39,802 --> 00:44:42,339
- Amalie. Pernille. 
- Yes.

389
00:44:42,430 --> 00:44:44,842
- Mariam. Eline. 
- Yes.

390
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:46,639
- Marcus. 
- He is sick.

391
00:44:50,563 --> 00:44:54,352
Okay. Olivia. Maya Emma. Nora.

392
00:44:54,442 --> 00:44:55,853
Then we go in.

393
00:45:21,928 --> 00:45:25,967
Anita H 09:31 
How is the shape?

394
00:45:49,330 --> 00:45:52,743
There is something not right.

395
00:45:52,833 --> 00:45:54,540
Okay?

396
00:45:57,296 --> 00:46:00,038
- Haven't you noticed? 
- No.

397
00:46:00,132 --> 00:46:01,998
What would it be?

398
00:46:11,686 --> 00:46:16,271
A link.

399
00:46:22,655 --> 00:46:24,692
Fin.

400
00:46:24,782 --> 00:46:28,070
That was what was missing.

401
00:46:30,746 --> 00:46:33,784
We have to leave.

402
00:46:33,874 --> 00:46:35,490
I'm coming.

403
00:46:46,095 --> 00:46:48,803
You are a little absent.

404
00:46:50,516 --> 00:46:53,053
- Do you think? 
- Yes, I do.

405
00:46:53,144 --> 00:46:55,806
Okay, no.

406
00:46:55,896 --> 00:46:58,638
Maybe I'm just a little tired.

407
00:47:00,067 --> 00:47:04,402
- Who are you texting all the time? 
- Just school stuff.

408
00:47:04,530 --> 00:47:07,363
School stuff? What then?

409
00:47:09,285 --> 00:47:12,823
A colleague who has 
problem with a student.

410
00:47:12,913 --> 00:47:16,122
A colleague? Who is that?

411
00:47:17,376 --> 00:47:20,994
- Her name is Elisabeth. 
- Elisabeth?

412
00:47:22,131 --> 00:47:24,372
What is the problem?

413
00:47:24,508 --> 00:47:29,548
It's boring to talk about. 
She asks if I have any advice.

414
00:47:29,638 --> 00:47:33,176
Does she ask you for advice? A new teacher.

415
00:47:35,770 --> 00:47:38,888
I'm looking forward to Budapest. 
It will be lovely.

416
00:47:38,981 --> 00:47:41,143
It had been a long time since we were there.

417
00:47:43,069 --> 00:47:44,901
Thank you.

418
00:47:45,029 --> 00:47:46,736
How many will we be?

419
00:47:46,822 --> 00:47:49,189
It's just us in the department.

420
00:47:49,283 --> 00:47:51,695
So a bunch of lawyers and me?

421
00:47:51,786 --> 00:47:54,904
No, most of them 
have had enough with their partners.

422
00:47:55,664 --> 00:47:58,782
Can you refrain from saying 
that you started working?

423
00:47:58,876 --> 00:48:00,867
- Why that? 
- Hey there.

424
00:48:01,003 --> 00:48:03,916
Hello, nice.

425
00:48:04,048 --> 00:48:06,631
Why that?

426
00:48:06,717 --> 00:48:09,835
This is Sofia, our new lawyer.

427
00:48:09,929 --> 00:48:12,170
- Anita. 
- Sofie, nice.

428
00:48:12,264 --> 00:48:14,301
Henriette is a co-owner.

429
00:48:14,392 --> 00:48:17,760
- Anita. 
- Nice to meet you, Anita.

430
00:48:19,063 --> 00:48:23,432
- Haven't you met? 
- I don't think so.

431
00:48:23,567 --> 00:48:26,309
You have been with us for a long time.

432
00:48:26,404 --> 00:48:30,523
- Four years? 
- Five years now.

433
00:48:30,658 --> 00:48:32,569
It's a long time.

434
00:48:32,660 --> 00:48:38,030
We work closely together. 
You were in Frankfurt last time.

435
00:48:38,124 --> 00:48:40,240
Very good lawyer, 
I must say.

436
00:48:40,376 --> 00:48:45,997
It was nice to meet. 
I have heard very good things.

437
00:48:48,092 --> 00:48:50,129
How was it in Davos, Henriette?

438
00:48:50,261 --> 00:48:52,844
It was actually absolutely fantastic.

439
00:48:52,930 --> 00:48:55,797
Anita 
Did you get my message?

440
00:48:55,891 --> 00:48:57,802
I was just supposed to work.

441
00:48:59,437 --> 00:49:04,728
I actually thought we should 
have our conference there.

442
00:49:04,859 --> 00:49:08,022
It's altitude training 
to just lie in the hotel.

443
00:49:08,112 --> 00:49:10,103
It's very loud, the hotel.

444
00:49:10,197 --> 00:49:12,564
- What did you say? 
- It seems to be high.

445
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:15,158
It was at 2000.

446
00:49:15,244 --> 00:49:18,157
It's actually loud.

447
00:49:18,247 --> 00:49:22,411
- How was training? 
- How was training?

448
00:49:22,543 --> 00:49:26,036
Legs feel heavy, 
but it is so beautiful.

449
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:29,205
Who did you train with?

450
00:49:30,634 --> 00:49:32,625
With Marianne and them.

451
00:49:33,637 --> 00:49:36,049
You haven't joined yet?

452
00:49:36,140 --> 00:49:38,723
Where were we last year? Paris it was.

453
00:49:38,809 --> 00:49:43,144
- It's a wonderful city. 
- Yes, incredibly nice.

454
00:49:43,230 --> 00:49:44,971
The Eiffel Tower and...

455
00:49:46,901 --> 00:49:49,689
Paris was absolutely fantastic.

456
00:49:49,778 --> 00:49:55,364
The trip was brilliant, 
but it would be fun to do something new.

457
00:49:55,451 --> 00:49:57,283
Marcus 
I have never felt better

458
00:49:57,369 --> 00:49:59,235
Or so I thought...

459
00:49:59,330 --> 00:50:02,072
- The babysitter? 
- No.

460
00:50:02,166 --> 00:50:03,782
Paid more?

461
00:50:03,876 --> 00:50:06,288
It's just work stuff.

462
00:50:10,716 --> 00:50:12,878
How long have you been married?

463
00:50:13,010 --> 00:50:15,718
- Hasse and me? 
- No.

464
00:50:15,804 --> 00:50:19,422
- Yes, Hasse and you. 
- Five years until the fall.

465
00:50:19,558 --> 00:50:21,970
Five years? It's not that long.

466
00:50:22,061 --> 00:50:24,143
Not by and large.

467
00:50:26,524 --> 00:50:28,185
Are you pregnant?

468
00:50:28,275 --> 00:50:30,642
No, I'm not.

469
00:50:30,778 --> 00:50:33,520
- I just... 
- No, then.

470
00:50:33,614 --> 00:50:36,652
- Would you like a glass of wine? 
- No, thanks.

471
00:50:41,872 --> 00:50:44,239
Did you meet on the Danmarksferjan?

472
00:50:44,375 --> 00:50:47,367
No, we met online.

473
00:50:47,503 --> 00:50:50,416
- Where? 
- Online.

474
00:50:51,882 --> 00:50:53,418
Online.

475
00:50:54,426 --> 00:50:58,135
They met online. 
That kind of online dating.

476
00:50:58,222 --> 00:51:00,714
Was it an app, or?

477
00:51:00,808 --> 00:51:06,099
You post a profile 
and see if anyone matches.

478
00:51:06,188 --> 00:51:10,307
- Isn't it just about lying down? 
- No.

479
00:51:10,401 --> 00:51:13,109
The one I want to sleep with, 
I agree with that.

480
00:51:13,195 --> 00:51:14,606
Isn't that so?

481
00:51:14,738 --> 00:51:17,400
Hasse, I'm just going to the bathroom.

482
00:51:17,533 --> 00:51:19,740
Surely that's good?

483
00:51:20,411 --> 00:51:24,075
Is there such an app 
for a father of five?

484
00:51:29,003 --> 00:51:32,746
Hi, it's Markus. 
I can't answer right now.

485
00:51:39,179 --> 00:51:41,420
I just have to go for a ride.

486
00:52:01,368 --> 00:52:04,201
- Hi:. 
- Hello.

487
00:52:04,288 --> 00:52:06,825
- Hello. 
- How cool you are.

488
00:52:06,915 --> 00:52:09,156
Tack.

489
00:52:09,251 --> 00:52:13,620
Actually, I'm out with my husband.

490
00:52:13,714 --> 00:52:17,378
I just wanted to talk to Markus.

491
00:52:17,509 --> 00:52:20,297
- He wasn't at school today. 
- Wasn't he?

492
00:52:20,387 --> 00:52:23,755
Didn't you know that?

493
00:52:23,849 --> 00:52:26,637
Another student said he was sick.

494
00:52:26,727 --> 00:52:28,593
No, I don't think so.

495
00:52:30,356 --> 00:52:34,145
At least he missed 
compulsory education.

496
00:52:34,234 --> 00:52:40,480
It's stupid in high school and 
we have an exam in that subject next week.

497
00:52:40,616 --> 00:52:42,072
And...

498
00:52:42,159 --> 00:52:47,529
- I just wanted to inform him. 
- Now he is in training.

499
00:52:47,623 --> 00:52:50,115
- What training? 
- On the football field.

500
00:52:50,209 --> 00:52:53,122
The one at school? Okay.

501
00:52:53,212 --> 00:52:56,750
We're going to the cinema 
and see Almodovar's latest.

502
00:52:56,840 --> 00:53:00,799
- "The Flesh of Love." 
- Med Palma de Rossy.

503
00:53:00,886 --> 00:53:05,881
I'll go there and tell you. 
No problem.

504
00:53:13,607 --> 00:53:16,770
- Excuse me? Have you seen Markus? 
- No.

505
00:53:16,860 --> 00:53:20,228
Long, dark, short hair. 
Plays in the junior team.

506
00:53:20,322 --> 00:53:23,189
- Isn't he with Robin? 
- He probably went to the port.

507
00:53:37,047 --> 00:53:39,755
- Are you sure? 
- Yes.

508
00:53:39,842 --> 00:53:42,300
Absolutely sure?

509
00:53:45,764 --> 00:53:49,803
I just...fell in love.

510
00:53:51,729 --> 00:53:55,438
It's not a big deal, 
I take one step at a time.

511
00:53:59,236 --> 00:54:01,068
Just like…

512
00:54:03,657 --> 00:54:05,739
I just have to…

513
00:54:08,579 --> 00:54:10,195
- Hi:. 
- Hello.

514
00:54:10,289 --> 00:54:13,247
- Thank you for last time. 
